  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved food and livelihood security in Bangladesh (BUET)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is part of a programme in which four Bangladeshi partners are collaborating together in order to address food and livelihood insecurity, which were identified as the key problems in Bagerhat district.  The International Training Network (ITN), a branch of the Bangladesh University of Engineering and Technology (BUET), is contributing technical advice and training on the assembly and function of solar panels, and testing of solar-based water purification systems.  ITN is also keeping beneficiaries informed about plans for the Bangladeshi government, in conjunction with the main mobile phone companies, to establish a system for sending out early warning alerts for cyclones and floods to all mobile phone users in coastal districts.</narrative>
  </description>
